# Every checkout gets the bytes that were committed: LF, on every OS.
#
# The knowledge map (docs/repo-map.json) records a SHA-256 of every tracked
# file, and tests/test_repo_map.py fails when a file no longer matches. A
# clone whose Git rewrote line endings on checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the
# default on a Windows runner) would make every file "changed" and the map
# stale on one OS while current on another. Pinning LF here keeps the hash
# the same everywhere, which is what lets CI run the same check on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf
